From: OpenAI Codex <noreply@openai.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: mt7996: write only allocated coredump sections

When memory dumping is disabled, or the chip has no memory layout, the
buffer contains only the fixed coredump header. Writing the memory section
length unconditionally writes four bytes beyond the requested allocation.

Use the same condition for constructing and allocating the memory section.

Signed-off-by: OpenAI Codex <noreply@openai.com>
---
 mt7996/coredump.c | 7 ++++---
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/mt7996/coredump.c b/mt7996/coredump.c
--- a/mt7996/coredump.c
+++ b/mt7996/coredump.c
@@ -202,11 +202,12 @@ static struct mt7996_coredump *mt7996_coredump_build(struct mt7996_dev *dev)
 	mt7996_coredump_fw_stack(dev, dump, exception);
 
 	/* gather memory content */
-	dump_mem = (struct mt7996_coredump_mem *)(buf + sofar);
-	dump_mem->len = crash_data->memdump_buf_len;
-	if (coredump_memdump && crash_data->memdump_buf_len)
+	if (coredump_memdump && crash_data->memdump_buf_len) {
+		dump_mem = (struct mt7996_coredump_mem *)(buf + sofar);
+		dump_mem->len = crash_data->memdump_buf_len;
 		memcpy(dump_mem->data, crash_data->memdump_buf,
 		       crash_data->memdump_buf_len);
+	}
 
 	mutex_unlock(&dev->dump_mutex);
 
